  </item>
  <item rdf:about="https://jvndb.jvn.jp/en/contents/2026/JVNDB-2026-099999.html">
    <title>KUSANAGI vulnerable to HTTP header injection</title>
    <link>https://jvndb.jvn.jp/en/contents/2026/JVNDB-2026-099999.html</link>
    <description>KUSANAGI provided by GMO Prime Strategy Co., Ltd. contains the following vulnerability in a redirect rule included in the Nginx configuration for WordPress:&lt;a href='https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/113.html' target='_blank'&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Improper Neutralization of CRLF Sequences in HTTP Headers (CWE-113) - &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;GMO Prime Strategy Co., Ltd. reported this vulnerability to JPCERT/CC to notify users of its solution through JVN. GMO Prime Strategy Co., Ltd. and JPCERT/CC coordinated under the Information Security Early Warning Partnership.</description>
    <sec:identifier>JVNDB-2026-099999</sec:identifier>
    <sec:references source="JVN" id="JVNVU#92635551">https://jvn.jp/en/vu/JVNVU92635551/index.html</sec:references>
    <sec:references title="HTTP Response Splitting(CWE-113)" id="CWE-113">https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/113.html</sec:references>
    <sec:cvss version="3.0" score="6.1" type="Base" severity="Medium" vector="CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N"/>
    <dc:date>2026-11-13T13:54+09:00</dc:date>
    <dcterms:issued>2026-11-10T15:55+09:00</dcterms:issued>
    <dcterms:modified>2026-11-13T13:54+09:00</dcterms:modified>
    <sec:foo>x</sec:foo>
  </item>
